despite its age the Nintendo switch is  still going strong we saw games that  appealed to almost every kind of  Nintendo fan from Kirby and the  Forgotten land to Xenoblade Chronicles  3. here are gamespot's 5 best Nintendo  switch games of 2022 and a few honorable  mentions at the end for good measure  before we get going keep in mind that  these games are in no particular order  [Music]  Mario plus Rabbids Kingdom battle was a  bizarre mashup of Nintendo's Mario  ubisoft's Rapids and XCOM like combat it  worked incredibly well despite its  disparate elements but the follow-up  proved itself much more than a mere  iterative sequel Mario plus Rabbids  Sparks of Hope is an improvement in  every meaningful way borrowing just  enough Mario DNA to make a tactical  experience that's unique to the genre  the most obvious difference is the  free-flowing movement allowing you to  run around the battlefield almost like  you would in a traditional Mario  platformer at first this change may seem  superficial but it actually has a  profound impact on gameplay allowing you  to chain your squad's moves one after  another to gain a tactical advantage  over your foes the spark system 2 gives  you an enormous amount of flexibility  over your team composition and strategy  for an experience unlike any other game  in its type Steve Watts wrote in his  review put simply Mario plus rapid  Sparks of Hope is an absolute Delight  this is a combination that shouldn't  work and yet it more than works it  excels  with its hybrid combination of TV and  portable functionality the Nintendo  switch is an ideal venue for deep midi  RPG experiences it doesn't get much more  substantial than Xenoblade Chronicles 3  the latest Epic from monolith soft the  sprawling tale of Warring Nations  tackles themes of sacrifice and  community and while its delivery is  sometimes held back by awkward dialogue  it's enough to care deeply about these  characters once the story hits its  stride equally ambitious is the revised  combat system with 23 classes and  unlockable Master Arts that add an extra  layer of tactical flexibility a  streamlined menu system makes it easy to  manage your mmo-like party and the  result is a system that rewards  experimentation as you play with  different party compositions and  loadouts that level of complexity gives  the experience its longevity as a  reviewer me I'm the reviewer still found  new options in master Arts after 120  hours in one of Nintendo's most  recognizable mascot characters Kirby has  seen his fair share of Platformers along  with more experimental projects on  handheld platforms like the Nintendo DS  even so the little pink puffball still  managed to surprise us this year with  Kirby and the Forgotten land the more  open structured platformer is akin to  the Mario 3D Land and World Games with  diorama-like environments filled with  challenges and obstacles to overcome  this time the world is built to look  more realistic with Real World objects  like traffic cones and even cars for  Kirby to gobble down when he takes on a  particularly large object he transforms  into mouthful mode a clever way to get  new gameplay functionality out of his  classic eating mechanic not only that  but the game also gives us upgradable  versions of many of the classic Kirby  power-ups you don't have to settle for a  little flame ability anymore as you can  become a lava spewing Terror instead it  all culminates in one of the wildest  endings in a Kirby game to date showing  the character still has some tricks up  its sleeve does Kirby have sleeves you  get the idea Pokemon fans got not just  one but two major Pokemon releases this  year and they were each special in their  own way in our opinion though the  standout was Pokemon Legends Arceus a  prequel that takes place in an era  inspired by the Japanese colonization  period the new setting allowed for a  very different take on the Pokemon  formula including a semi-open world  structure full of sprawling environments  to explore rather than the traditional  quest of catching wild Pokemon and  raising to the ranks of Pokemon Master  Arceus put you in the role of a Pokemon  researcher this meant completing  research tasks like defeating a certain  number of Pokemon capturing a certain  type and more the gameplay changed to  facilitate this new take on the Pokemon  Norm with the ability to catch Pokemon  in the Wild by simply tossing a Pokeball  without being seen it makes stealth  traditional Pokemon mechanics and  exploration into a package that was hard  to resist  Wii Sports was a genuine phenomenon that  we don't see in video games the type of  breakout success that inspires  mainstream press attention and finds its  way into the lives of non-traditional  Gamers it only makes sense that Nintendo  would follow up on the switch with its  joy-con functionality acting very  similar to the Wii remote Nintendo  switch Sports is the result a new  package that brings back popular sports  like bowling and Tennis alongside new  events like badminton soccer volleyball  and chimbara like the best social games  switch Sports is best if you can gather  a bunch of friends together to complete  goals knock each other around in an epic  sword duel and more and Nintendo has  made a habit of committing continuing  support to games like this as it  recently added golf to the switch Sports  repertoire it's a great little package  that scratches the itch that made the  Wii Sports such a hit Kurt and Davina  wrote in gamespot's Nintendo switch  Sports review Nintendo switch Sports is  a fantastic multiplayer game that for  the most part invites anyone and  everyone to pick up a controller and  flail their limbs about it has its  issues but they fall away when you have  other people to play with and are  joyously going Toe to Toe in Virtual  Sports as with the original Wii Sports  Nintendo switch Sports finds Beauty and  fun and simplicity and bullying is great  better than real life bowling all right  with that out of the way let's get to  the honorable mentions why don't we  start with the Nintendo exclusives  Nintendo's colorful multiplayer shooter  Splatoon returned in 2022. Splatoon 3  had the same infectious charm as its  predecessors but packed it with a ton of  new and returning content if you're  looking for a vibrant and original take  on the competitive shooter genre then  look no further along with splatting the  competition you'll need to Ink the  playing field in order to win in  addition to the tried and true  multiplayer modes Splatoon 3 also has a  robust single player campaign with some  excellent boss fights and a bite-size  wave defense mode called Salmon Run  let's drop another third entry in this  list and highlight Bayonetta 3.  Bayonetta 3 is platinum games at its  peak this Multiverse hopping character  action game is explosive Adventure chock  full of colorful characters hectic set  pieces and ridiculous weapons including  a train sword or a sword train depending  on how you want to look at it its  visuals do suffer a bit but the Absurd  action and bayonetta's Charming wit more  than makes up for its technical hiccups  Mario has starred in countless party and  sports games but they are almost never  as technically complex and skill testing  as Mario Striker's battle League this  game pits the Mushroom Kingdom All-Stars  against each other in a wild soccer bout  complete with various pieces of  armor-like equipment to Dawn and big  flourishes in the form of unlockable  shots while the content offering is a  bit anemic compared to the best Mario  sports games this is one for the fans  who take their virtual footy seriously  and want to prove it out on the pitch  card shark developed by nerial and  published by devolver digital is an  adventure game that has you cheating  your way to success it takes place in  18th century France and boasts a  colorful art style of course there is a  lot more going on in the story than  meets the eye if this Peaks your  interest I highly recommend checking out  the free demo on the Nintendo switch  storefront a lot has already been said  about near automata at this point many  consider it one of the best games in the  last few years and now you can play it  on switch typically we try to stick to  new releases for our best of the Year  coverage but we were blown away by how  well this port runs on the little hybrid  console if you haven't had the chance to  check out this Platinum Games gem  consider this a sign  there it is our favorite Nintendo switch  games of 2022 and 5 honorable mentions  this should be more than enough to keep  you busy over the holiday season let us  know your favorite switch games in the  comments below and with that we'll see  you next time  [Music]
 

